POLICY:
I will not disclose any information shared with me in confidence for any purpose unless their is a ethical requirement to do so(eg: disclosing live-exploitable vulnerabilities, abuse, or corruption) or doing so would prevent actionable, signifigant, and imminent harm to self or others. I will not discuss information shared with me for purposes of peer counseling, psychologic first aid, or identity validation for  any purpose other than preventing actional, signifigant, and immentint harm to self or others.


I will not sign at full validity any PGP keys that do not meet one of the following criteria, or are weaker than RSA-2048. I will not sign at marginal validity any key that does not pass email varification, is weaker than RSA-2048, or cannot present 1 recognizable form of ID. 
1. Belong to me
2. Belong to someone I know personally and trust, and have confirmed the fingerprint and email verbally with them and with a test message requiring them to decrypt a message sent to their email, find the phrase within, and sign an email with both that phrase and one we discussed
3. Belong to a person who has verified their identity with 2 forms of identification, one of which must be a government-issued photo ID, and have confirmed the fingerprint and email verbally with them and with a test message requiring them to decrypt a message sent to their email, find the phrase within, and sign an email with both that phrase and one we discussed
4. Belong to a person who has verified their identity with 1 form of identification, who was introduced to me by someone I trust, have provided a reason for lack of a second form of identification/identification that is not a government photo ID, and have confirmed the fingerprint and email verbally with them and with a test message requiring them to decrypt a message sent to their email, find the phrase within, and sign an email with both that phrase and one we discussed
5. Belong to an organization I am affiliated with or am a member of, provided a document pgp-signed by 3 or more members I have verified keys for and know or have verified have authorization to create an organizational PGP key, be associated with a non-individual email address associated with that organization’s domain, and have confirmed the fingerprint and email verbally with them and with a test message requiring them to decrypt a message sent to their email, find the phrase within, and sign an email with both that phrase and one we discussed
6. Belong to an organization, provided a document pgp-signed by 3 or more members I have verified keys for and know or have verified have authorization to create an organizational PGP key, have confirmed veracity to create key via a combination of documentation and verification that satisfies any reasonable concerns of unauthorized key creation, be associated with a non-individual email address associated with that organization’s domain, and have confirmed the fingerprint and email verbally with them and with a test message requiring them to decrypt a message sent to their email, find the phrase within, and sign an email with both that phrase and one we discussed
7. Belong to an organization known to me, be introduced to me by 3 individuals I trust, be a publicly known member of  that organization, provide an authorization document pgp-signed by 5 or more members of that organization, present a physical copy of that authorization document on organizational letterhead signed by those same 5 or more members, have confirmed veracity to create key via a combination of documentation and verification that satisfies any reasonable concerns of unauthorized key creation, be associated with a non-individual email address associated with that organization’s domain, and have confirmed the fingerprint and email verbally with them and with a test message requiring them to decrypt a message sent to their email, find the phrase within, and sign an email with both that phrase and one we discussed


My web of trust values remain at default. I will use marginal ownertrust to indicate someone who meets one of my conditions to deny full ownertrust, but otherwise has rigorous trust and validity standards. Any person with a defined rigorous process that does not have 1 of the following issues, that I personally and professionally trust to validate and trust keys rigorously, and is either someone I trust ultimately[1], is confirmed as trustworthy by 1 person i trust ultimately[2], or is confirmed as trustworthy by 3 people that I trust fully[3].
1. Signs keys smaller than RSA 2048
2. Does not have a published and signed document outlining trust and validity standards
3. Uses a standard lower  than mine in a matter of significance(differences in acceptable ID docs, acceptable key length for marginal validity, or organizational key requirements are acceptable)


I will not sign keys irrevocably or with trust signatures.


I will not publish software, or release updates to software, without a PGP signature. Daily and weekly automatic builds are excluded from this.


If you require further identity verification, please send me a pgp-encrypted message to whichever of my accounts you are most comfortable reaching out to, and we can discuss further verification


